# Cursor rules — pointer file

Modern Cursor reads structured rules from `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`. This file is
kept only for older Cursor clients that do not yet read that directory.

Read these in order:
1. `AGENTS.md` — agent-facing guide for the whole repo
2. `.cursor/rules/repo-conventions.mdc` — always-on conventions
3. `.cursor/rules/prompt-discipline.mdc` — rules for executing prompts from the Prompt Library
4. `.cursor/rules/context-files.mdc` — rules for never editing AGENTS.md / CLAUDE.md / .cursor/

## Quick conventions

- pnpm workspace monorepo. pnpm 10, Node 22+ (CI and Render both pin Node 22 — match locally). Squash merges into `main`.
- This repo is **backend automation only** — no UI, no React, no Vite. Do not install UI frameworks.
- All planning docs live in `docs/ways-of-work/plan/content-pipeline-v2/`. **`docs/` is read-only.**
- All implementation work comes from prompts in `docs/ways-of-work/plan/content-pipeline-v2/cursor-claude-prompt-library.md`. **One prompt = one PR.**
- **Never edit** `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, or anything under `.cursor/`, `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`, `.editorconfig`, `.gitignore`. These are strategist-authored. If a behavior change is needed, stop and add a `// TODO(hassan):` note in the PR description.
- Never use the words "scrape" or "crawl" — use "collect", "extract", "browse", "read".
- TypeScript strict mode. No `any`. All async wrapped in try/catch with `lib/logger`.
- No `.env` files committed. Real env vars live in Render and Cursor Cloud / local shell.
- No new top-level dependencies, no version bumps, no lib/db schema changes outside the active prompt's allowlist.
- PR title format: `Prompt N: <short description>`. PR description follows `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`.
